# =============================================================================
# .gitignore for the RoBMA 4.0 rigor-estimand pipeline repository
# =============================================================================
#
# Policy (see docs/output_commit_policy.md for the authoritative list):
#   - COMMIT:    source code (scripts/, simulation/scripts/), documentation
#                (docs/, README.md, scripts/README.md, simulation/README*.md,
#                CITATION.cff, LICENSE*), data inputs (data/<stratum>/*.csv,
#                *.xlsx), per-stratum sidecars
#                (output/<stratum>/<stratum>_robma_summary.csv,
#                _zplot_diagnostics.csv), the v4 overview tables/figures
#                under output/overview/, per-source audit CSVs and z-plot
#                PDFs under output/<stratum>/<source>/.
#   - IGNORE:    fitted model objects (*.rds / *.Rds / *.RData), the entire
#                simulation output tree (output_sim_v30/, simulation/results/),
#                the heavy RoBMA-3.6 archive snapshot, atomic-rename leftovers
#                (*.bak), local R/editor/OS junk.
#
# To opt a normally-ignored file IN (e.g., a single representative fit, or a
# sim summary CSV you decide to ship), force-add it:
#     git add -f <path>
# =============================================================================


# ---- R session & history ----------------------------------------------------
.Rhistory
.Rapp.history
.RData
.Ruserdata
.Rproj.user/
*.Rproj


# ---- R package build / check artifacts --------------------------------------
*.Rcheck/
*.tar.gz
*-Ex.R


# ---- R caches ---------------------------------------------------------------
.Rcache/
.cache/
*_cache/


# ---- renv: INTENTIONALLY INACTIVE during active development -----------------
# The pipeline uses the plain R user library, not renv. Stale renv infra
# was archived to archive/renv_inactive_<date>/ (small, intentionally
# tracked for provenance). The authoritative environment record is
# docs/environment.md. Ignore any accidentally-regenerated renv artifacts
# at the repo root so a stray renv run is never silently tracked.
/renv/
/renv.lock
/.Rprofile
# Also ignore renv library/staging anywhere they might appear:
**/renv/library/
**/renv/staging/
**/renv/local/
**/renv/lock.json


# ---- Heavy model objects (regenerable; never shipped by default) ------------
# Every fit and zplot artifact written by 20_robma_fit.R is an *.rds:
#   fit_RE4_*.rds, fit_RoBMA4_*.rds, zplot_RE4_*.rds, zplot_RoBMA4_*.rds.
# Documented summary artifacts are CSV / PDF / PNG / TEX — never RDS — so
# a global *.rds ignore is safe across this repo.
*.rds
*.Rds
*.RData
*.rda


# ---- Active generated simulation output roots -------------------------------
# Release decision (locked at v1.0.0): the public GitHub release ships
# simulation source, design grid, and runbooks but NOT the generated
# synthetic datasets, fitted simulation outputs, or simulation result trees.
# All are regenerable from the included scripts + design CSV + recorded
# R / JAGS environment. See docs/output_commit_policy.md for the full rule.
output_sim_v30/
simulation/results/
simulation/results_archive*/

# Generated synthetic input datasets (~18,000 CSVs at n_reps = 500) and
# their latent / manifest provenance. Regenerable end-to-end from
# simulation/config/design_v3_full36.csv + the fixed generation seed in
# simulation/scripts/20_sim_generate.R via sim_generate_library(n_reps).
# Ignored as a release-policy guard so a casual `git add .` from the repo
# root cannot accidentally stage them. To regenerate locally: see
# simulation/README.md and docs/runbook.md (Phase B).
data/sim_*/
simulation/latent/
simulation/manifests/

# Heavy raw-draws CSVs that exceed GitHub's 100-MB-per-file limit. Belt-and-
# braces in case simulation/results/ ever becomes selectively tracked.
simulation/results/**/*_size_curve_draws.csv
simulation/results/empirical_resampling/empirical_resampling_size_curve.csv

# Local probe scratch under any output root.
output*/_scratch/


# ---- Heavy archives (provenance only; not shipped) --------------------------
# archive/ is the retirement yard. Small README/lineage files inside it
# remain commit-eligible, but the heavy RoBMA-3.6 snapshot (~70 GB) must
# never be committed. Generic guards catch any per-archive output/results/
# library trees that someone might drop in later.
archive/RoBMA_3_6/
archive/**/output*/
archive/**/results*/
archive/**/library/
archive/**/staging/


# ---- Local-only / scratch ---------------------------------------------------
scratch/
tmp/
*.tmp
*.bak
*.swp
*.swo
*~
Rplots.pdf
~$*.xlsx
~$*.xls


# ---- Internal / planning artifacts (local-only, never shipped) --------------
# Repo-cleanup audits, scratch design notes, and other internal planning
# material. The leading underscore is the convention for "internal" in this
# repo; keep it consistent if new internal folders are added.
_repo_cleanup/


# ---- Editor / IDE -----------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.code-workspace


# ---- OS noise ---------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini


# ---- LaTeX build artifacts (manuscript/ keeps .tex and .pdf) ----------------
manuscript/**/*.aux
manuscript/**/*.log
manuscript/**/*.out
manuscript/**/*.toc
manuscript/**/*.lof
manuscript/**/*.lot
manuscript/**/*.bbl
manuscript/**/*.blg
manuscript/**/*.fls
manuscript/**/*.fdb_latexmk
manuscript/**/*.synctex.gz
manuscript/**/*.run.xml


# ---- Logs -------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
batch_status_*.csv


# =============================================================================
# NOTES on rules that USED to be here and were removed
# =============================================================================
# - output/**/fit_RE_*.rds, output/**/fit_RoBMA_*.rds,
#   output/**/zcurve_RE_*.rds, output/**/zcurve_RoBMA_*.rds,
#   output/**/*.rds                  -> superseded by global *.rds above
# - output/**/**/plots/               REMOVED: this rule incorrectly ignored
#                                     the manuscript-relevant per-source
#                                     z-plot PDFs at
#                                     output/<stratum>/<source>/plots/*.pdf,
#                                     which are intended public artifacts
#                                     per docs/output_contract.md §1.
# - output/**/**/summary/             REMOVED: no /summary/ subdir is written
#                                     by the active pipeline.
